mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# STONE & LEAF — Backend API\n\nBackend for the STONE & LEAF private viewing studio. Visitors submit a private\nviewing request; the studio owner retrieves submitted requests. Open to Visit ·\nCome by the Studio — everyone is welcome to drop in and explore.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nThe backend uses Internet Identity. A caller is identified by the principal\nderived from their Internet Identity delegation.\n\n- `submitViewingRequest` is open to any caller, including anonymous callers.\n- `listViewingRequests` requires an admin (studio owner) caller. A non-admin\n  caller receives a trap: `Unauthorized: Only the studio owner can view requests`.\n- `getCallerUserRole` returns the caller's role (`#admin`, `#user`, or `#guest`).\n- `assignCallerUserRole` and `isCallerAdmin` are provided by the authorization\n  component; the first caller to initialize access control becomes the admin.\n\nThe app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the\nuser's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal\nagainst that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`).\nSuch a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it\nexpires.\n\nRegistration is required before role-guarded calls. A direct API caller must\ncall `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any\nrole-guarded call, including guarded queries. The first initializer receives the\n`#admin` role; subsequent callers receive `#user`. An unregistered or anonymous\ncaller on a guarded endpoint receives the trap\n`Unauthorized: Only the studio owner can view requests`. A caller can be\nunregistered even when the app already knows them: registration happens only\nwhen a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never\ndid so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in\ncaller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one\nthe frontend registered.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `submitViewingRequest(input : ViewingRequestInput) : async SubmitResult`\n\nSubmits a private viewing request. `input` carries `name`, `email`, `phone`,\n`preferredDate`, and `message`, all `Text`. All fields are required and are\ntrimmed of surrounding spaces before storage. `email` must contain exactly one\n`@` with a non-empty local part and a domain containing a `.`.\n\nReturns `SubmitResult`:\n- `#ok(ViewingRequest)` — the stored request, including its assigned `id` and\n  `submittedAt` timestamp.\n- `#err([ValidationError])` — one or more of `#nameRequired`, `#emailRequired`,\n  `#emailInvalid`, `#phoneRequired`, `#preferredDateRequired`,\n  `#messageRequired`. Nothing is stored when validation fails.\n\nThis is an update call. Retrying a successful submission creates a new request\nwith a new `id`; it is not idempotent.\n\n### `listViewingRequests() : async [ViewingRequest]`\n\nReturns every stored viewing request. Admin (studio owner) only; a non-admin\ncaller traps. This is a query call.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async Text`\n\nReturns this document. Query call, open to any caller.\n\n### `getCallerUserRole() : async UserRole`\n\nReturns the caller's role: `#admin`, `#user`, or `#guest`.\n\n### `isCallerAdmin() : async Bool`\n\nReturns whether the caller holds the `#admin` role.\n\n### `assignCallerUserRole(user : Principal, role : UserRole) : async ()`\n\nAdmin-only. Assigns a role to another principal.\n\n### `_initialize_access_control() : async ()`\n\nInitializes access control for the calling principal. The first caller becomes\n`#admin`; later callers become `#user`.\n\n### `_internet_identity_sign_in_start()` / `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish(...)`\n\nInternet Identity sign-in flow endpoints provided by the authorization\ncomponent.\n\n## Data model\n\n`ViewingRequest`:\n- `id : Nat` — sequential identifier assigned at submission.\n- `name : Text`\n- `email : Text`\n- `phone : Text`\n- `preferredDate : Text` — the visitor's preferred date, as free text.\n- `message : Text` — a short note about the project.\n- `submittedAt : Int` — nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (IC `Time.now()`).\n\n## OQL data exposure\n\nPersisted viewing requests are exposed to the Caffeine Data Intelligence agent\nthrough the Object Query Layer as the `viewingRequest` entity, keyed by `id`.\nThe entity is `controllerOnly`: the platform controller (and therefore the Data\nIntelligence agent) can read all rows, while end users cannot read the table\ndirectly. The `schema()` and `execute()` query endpoints are provided by the OQL\n`Expose` mixin.\n";
  };
};
